!! Operator Rulings — Current Working Copy

''Status:'' Annotated design copy. Preserves the existing Ichi record and all inherited mechanics except where later annotations explicitly supersede the original worked example. The branch-current original in `bags/elyncia/ha.ka.ba/elyncia/characters/primary-characters/ichi.mem` remains untouched.

''Source blob:'' `318dda385794535dddc5425fb03b861945074685` at ref `feature/lady-aki-character-sheet`.

* ''RULING:'' Ichi (he/them) holds Level 2 in his own right and stands as Aki's fully fledged deuteragonist, rather than an item owned by Aki. The Aki-Ichi bond lives in Social Inventory with mutual upkeep, agency and respect; physical armor interfaces and mode-switch rules remain subject to the existing Powered Symbiote mechanics.
* ''RULING:'' Ichi receives one personal ''Level 1 Hallmark'': ''Broken Isles Field Spade'' (working name). Choose the practical military spade direction; the exact single-ended vs crescent-headed geometry and one upgrade feature remain OPEN.
* ''RULING:'' Reconstructed kabuto, left gauntlet and right greave are present, modeled on surviving blueprints and fashioned from treated chitin shed during Aki's molts. These three components may later undergo recovery of original hardware and/or synthesis with reconstructed structures.
* ''RULING:'' Ichi's original tachi, asymmetrical bow and rifle are missing. The bokken and tantō stand as current paired fighting weapons. The yari belongs to his originally issued kit, but its survival and current location remain OPEN.
* ''OPEN:'' No established account yet explains the missing kit; possibilities include battlefield loss, looting, salvage or deliberate separation. Do not mark any hypothesis canon.
* ''OPEN:'' The recovered armor, shrine and associated hardware may contain de-leveled, locked, damaged, encrypted, corrupted or Vome-affected features. Diagnose each subsystem individually; higher power production alone does not repair missing hardware, clear corruption or grant extra purchased features.

''Accounting:'' Ichi's original sheet retains four occupied base Trait slots and four legacy equipment entries. The field spade adds a Level 1 invested Hallmark in Ichi's own gear inventory. Its proposed two-stone bulk and physical carriage must count separately; the revised ready-item/packed tally and XP source remain OPEN. No new automatic attacks, Armor/Ward, DT, Powers or free +1 roll are awarded.

