! Ichi (he/them) — Character Sheet

*Ichi and Aki serve as the book example for the Powered Symbiote trait.*

''Player:'' Freyja (also plays Lady Aki)
''Concept:'' Spore-daemon-armor symbiote — three things that merged into a person
''Heritage:'' Construct
''Level:'' 2
''Role:'' Deuteragonist; independent living construct-golem and military veteran, bonded to Aki as familiar/squire/symbiote through Social Inventory; autonomous fighter / DreamNet interface. This supersedes the legacy Hallmark-companion inventory wording for Ichi-as-person while retaining the Powered Symbiote rules as a mechanics reference.

---

!! Origin

!!! The Armor's Long Line

''Designed in the Faerie Court Wars'' (''YOLD ~3195–4200'' —
[[the-faerie-court-wars|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/concepts/the-faerie-court-wars]]). The powered
armor and its personal daemon-core came out of the clan wars of the settlement age: after the
Apophis Datum re-based the world's shores, while the human clan pressed its ascendancy across the
new geography, and ''before the Neo-Thracian Empire stood as a power at all''. Roughly two thousand
years before the present day.

''Found, then inherited, by a people already there.'' The clan that recovered the wreck reads
''native to the Broken Isles'' — a mostly-human-fae people of that ground, not incomers to it.
When the armor was made, their country was not islands at all: it stood as ''the eastern shelf of
Mu'', attached to the largest Nexus in the Western Net, coast of the drowned low kingdoms. The
clan held that shelf through the Court Wars and the two thousand years after, and the armor passed
down ''three generations'' among them — fae-blooded generations, which run long. The third wearer
carried it against the ''invading Neo-Thracian forces''.

''The year that took everything at once.'' YOLD 5000 did not deal this clan a defeat. It dealt them
three things in one season: the ''Necrospire's fall tore their shelf away from Mu'', leaving three
great islands split by Astral rifts where a coastline had been; a ''Neo-Thracian expedition'' was
fighting on their ground, several factional fronts at once, its supply chain already spent; and
then ''Web 2 died across the whole planet in a day''.

''They did not lose a battle. They lost the continent, the network, and the war together'' — and
the invaders lost with them, stranded at the farthest point from Neo-Thracia a soldier could stand.

''The name keeps the wound.'' Charts still read ''the Broken Isles''. The rift-coast locals say
''the Shattered Isles'', //and keep the older grief in it//. That grief is this clan's, and Ichi
was standing in it when the sky fell.

''What Ichi holds of it:'' the sky falling. The signal cutting out. Nothing after. Whether that
memory rides locked, extracted, burned, or otherwise, ''Ichi cannot tell from the inside'' — the
Burned Library's own condition, worn by a person instead of a shelf.

!!! The Waking

A floating Ephyra spore-jellyfish — a tasked spirit of the ''anchored Mother Spore cluster'' that
serves Lady Aki's priesthood in the settled Isles — went out on an ordinary errand: settle,
colonize, raise a batch of mushroom-ashigaru homunculi, send them home for jobs. Aki followed it
out past the cultivated ground into the fungal jungle, and it came down on a blast-scarred
roadside shrine with the armor still lying in the wreck beside it.

Instead of colonizing, the spore-jelly symbiosed with the daemon. Something woke up. Not a
homunculus, not a daemon, not a suit of armor — something new. //(The clearing's full event, and
what else woke in it, rides at
[[strandbeest-shrine|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/characters/companions/strandbeest-shrine]].)//

''The anomaly, named.'' A tasked spirit ''cannot exceed its assigned scope'' — the DreamNet's own
law. This one did. Whether the binding had decayed across the errand, or the waking shrine
re-bound it when it announced //re-routing mana// (a node holds the authority to bind tasked
spirits), or something else entirely, ''stands open''. Ichi therefore reads as neither miracle nor
malfunction but as a ''jurisdictional question with a person standing in it''.

---

!! Visual Description

''Silhouette:'' Compact, practical ashigaru infantry armor. Sergeant's kit — functional, not decorative. Medium humanoid frame, slightly stocky.

''Dō (cuirass):'' Hexagonal kikko-pattern plates of alchemically treated chitin — iridescent beetle-shell blues and greens — riveted to woven mycelium-silk backing. The joins pulse with faint ''orange bioluminescent tracery'' where the mycelial symbiont threads through the armor like living mortar.

''Kote (armored sleeves) & suneate (greaves):'' Lamellae of rare petrified hardwood, lacquered in dark amber resin, laced with silk cord in traditional odoshi style. Where millennia of dormancy cracked the wood, mycelium has filled the gaps with glowing orange scar-tissue.

''Kabuto (helmet):'' Open-faced sergeant's design — forged magical-metal-composite (orichalcum-alloyed bronze), modest shikoro neck guard of chitin lamellae. The face opening shows ''two glowing yellow-orange orbs'' — the daemon-spore consciousness looking out.

''When worn by Aki:'' The eye-spots migrate upward, settling above Aki's brow like a luminous crest — a guardian's gaze watching from above the wearer's face.

''Overall:'' The patina of something built to be used, not displayed. Cracks filled with light. Surfaces that breathe. A damaged thing made whole in a way its makers never intended.

---

!! Long-Watch Resonances!! Restoration of Three Reconstructed Armor Sections — RULING

The present ''kabuto'', ''left gauntlet'' and ''right greave'' carry functional reconstructed structures, made from surviving original armor blueprints using ''treated chitin naturally shed during Aki's molts''. These replacements account for the present helmet, sleeve/gauntlet, and greave descriptions; they do not imply the missing original components have been recovered.

| Current component | Present status | Future recovery or synthesis hook |
|---|---|---|
| Kabuto | Reconstructed and worn | Search for original helm components, recover separate legacy electronics/memories if evidence supports them, or integrate reconstructed chitin with safely restored hardware |
| Left gauntlet | Reconstructed and worn | Recover original gauntlet or make a considered composite; bow-hand/weapon-control function remains a hypothesis |
| Right greave | Reconstructed and worn | Recover original greave or synthesize powered bracing/mobility from surviving interface data; recoil stabilization remains a hypothesis |

''Preserve present defenses:'' Existing Armor, Ward, DT and Burn calculations describe Ichi's current playable body. Treat original component functions, old levels, missing slots, firmware status and any enhancement as OPEN, not automatically inherited from the blueprints. A recoverable component might restore familiar functionality, reveal locked data, or introduce hazards before anyone can safely integrate it.

''Synthesis is a choice:'' Ichi and Aki may retain repaired chitin, replace it, or integrate historical and living structures. The recovered originals need not erase the repairs or the relationship through which they grew.

---

!! Long-Watch Resonances

''Character-design references, not imported affiliations.'' Ichi shares Aki's resonance with the Redmane Army, the giants who kept guarding Anor Londo after glory passed, and the Blue Moon knights under Gwyndolyn. A soldier who keeps watch over ruins and a magical household carries those examples through service, repair, stubborn comradeship, and respect for the veiled protector. Ichi's friendly mycelial consciousness transforms old martial purpose into protection of living companions rather than mere obedience to an extinct army.

Ichi's scarred chitin, orange fungal light, and compact ashigaru form retain their established silhouette; the references guide conduct and atmosphere rather than replacing the armor with Soulsborne livery.

---

!! Ability Scores — The Dreamer

| STR | AGI | END | THT | CHA | AUR |
| 1 | 0 | 2 | 1 | 1 | 2 |

*Emphasis: Aura-heavy for Dreamwalker and DreamNet interfacing. Endurance for the ancient frame's stubbornness. Charisma and Thought for a nascent mind learning to be a person. Strength sufficient but not dominant — the daemon remembers fighting, but Ichi is more dreamer than warrior.*

