!! Life

''12'' — base 4 + 4/level across 2 Levels (standard track, matching Aki's). //(Re-spend stays open to Freyja's XP choices.)//

---

!! Heritage: Construct *(free, no trait slot)*

> Ichi is a Construct Golem, part modern Elyncian mycelial tasked spirit, part dreaming daemon, and part lost magitech powered armor from the Faerie Court Wars of the settlement age.

''Deathless'' //(Skilled slot 1)// — Ichi doesn't die at 0 Life. They enter a dormant state. Recovery requires upkeep: organic matter, mana-rich nutrients, ambient ley-line signal, or time at a functioning node. Sacrifice something to trigger reconstitution — biomass, a potion, a watch spent at a lararium.

''Armoured Body'' //(Skilled slot 2, +1 Armor, +1 Ward)// — The ancient chitin-and-composite plating. Inherent structural toughness — cannot be removed. \*This bonus applies in ''both'' autonomous and worn modes. In worn mode it is included in the base +5/+1 rating (exception to normal stacking; see Powered Symbiote core rules).

''Inner Fire'' //(Skilled, slot 3, +2 flexible inventory slots, +1 Defeat threshold)// — The daemon core refuses to go down. The two bonus slots are ''flexible'': assign each to the trait or item inventory as it fills (ruled: Inner Fire expands //any// inventory). For Ichi they represent integral compartments, sealed weapon mounts, and the mycelium dream-deck's internal footprint.

---

!! Traits (4/8 base slots; +2 Inner Fire flex shared with Gear)

''Slot count:'' 7 + THT 1 = ''8'' base trait slots. Four sit filled — Golem, Background: Military,
Powered Symbiote, Dreamwalker. Heritage Construct rides ''free'' and consumes none of them; its
three Skilled effects (Deathless, Armoured Body, Inner Fire) ride with the Heritage, not the
trait inventory. Inner Fire adds 2 flexible slots that Ichi may assign to either inventory as it
fills.

!!! Slot 0a — Golem *(Path trait)*

> "You have made, remade, and unmade yourself. You have a timelost civilian profession. You become Skilled (+3) in any activity you closely observe for a day, encoding it as a skill lemma stored in an inventory slot."

''Ichi's timelost profession:'' Sergeant's field maintenance — the daemon remembers how to repair kit, maintain a camp perimeter, check armor straps, organize a supply line. Fragmentary, practical, nothing glamorous.

''Skill-lemma encoding'' is Ichi's core learning mechanism: //watch, absorb, replicate//. The spore-jelly was designed to do exactly this. The daemon adds context — not just "how to sharpen a blade" but "how a soldier sharpens a blade before a battle they don't expect to survive."

---

!!! Slot 0b — Background: Military *(Court Wars sergeant)*

''Two military strata, and both stand playable.'' The daemon's own craft runs back to the ''Faerie Court Wars'' (YOLD ~3195–4200) — the armor is that old, and the sergeant's habits come with it: formation discipline, tactical assessment, field logistics, and recognition of rank insignia and command structures, ''including ancient and obsolete ones''. Its ''last'' service ran far younger: three generations in a mostly-human-fae Broken Isles clan, ending against the Neo-Thracian invasion in the year of the Fall (YOLD 5000).

''Why the second stratum matters at the table:'' the company sails for Neo-Thracia, and the kit, ranks, road-signs, camp habits, and siege-marks Ichi knows in his hands are ''that Nexus's own, from the losing side of an invasion''. He reads their architecture the way a veteran reads a rival regiment's trenches.

When Ichi encounters military architecture, fortifications, or unit formations from either era, the daemon's buried memory may surface as instinct or déjà vu.

