!!! Personal Hallmark — Broken Isles Field Spade (Level 1; selected)

''Status: RULING on choice and Level; PROVISIONAL on profile.'' Ichi carries a practical, combat-capable field spade as his own first invested Hallmark, separate from his originally issued yari, lost tachi, lost bow and lost rifle. The working name ''Broken Isles Field Spade'' may change in play.

* ''Form:'' Military field tool suitable for digging, clearing, bracing and guarding a passage. Study the historical crescent monk-spade and other martial implements without presuming a fully double-ended weapon. Exact head geometry remains OPEN.
* ''Baseline comparator (not yet finalized):'' 2 stone, two-handed, approximately 1d10 using the SDM Wrench Hammer reference. Referee to confirm damage, size, attack ability, readiness, and whether the item uses more than one of Ichi's physical item slots in ordinary carriage.
* ''Hallmark:'' Level 1 in Ichi's own Item inventory, not attached to Aki's Hallmark or Social Inventory. Its +1 item Level represents the Hallmark investment; it does not itself grant a bonus to attack rolls, damage, Armor, Ward or Trait. XP acquisition/source and item costs need a ledger decision.
* ''Combat use:'' Ordinary field-spade melee use follows the chosen baseline weapon rule; specialized reach, entanglement, control, magical warding and ritual abilities require specific paid upgrades or Powers.
* ''Work use:'' Appropriate for Ichi's existing Military field-maintenance and Golem Path work: road repair, camp preparation, excavation, clearing and civilian protection. The spade does not automatically confer a priestly Background or shrine Power.
* ''Logistics:'' Treat the spade as visible military-capable equipment in town, even when it performs civil work. Its 2-stone size and deployment may require appropriate carrying arrangements; no assumption of instant access from packed shrine cargo.

''Equipment tally OPEN:'' Prior baseline records 4/8 occupied Item entries and two Inner Fire flexible slots shared with Traits. Adding a two-stone Hallmark may demand two physical item slots, one of which serves as its Hallmark entry; a working 6/8 physical tally follows if all prior entries truly consume one stone apiece. The starter kit is grouped and requires an itemized ready/packed audit before using that total as final.



---

!! Friendly Mycelial Armament — Weapon Imbuement and Balefire

''Established fictional capability; numeric playtest accounting still open.'' Ichi's friendly mycelial symbiote can ''imbue weapons'' through its living spore-and-daemon substrate. The imbuement reads as a protective guardian's craft: old sergeant maintenance joined to the responsive fungal magic of Aki's mobile shrine. The SDM Power ''Imbue Edge'' offers a rules crosswalk, but this record does not yet assign Ichi that Power, its cost, or a free unlimited equivalent.

Ichi can also ''throw Balefire grenades'': chitin pots holding combustion powder and a toxic, sticky, magic-corroding flame. On release, Balefire clings to what it strikes and corrodes magical protections as well as threatening living matter. This describes the fictional effect, not a real-world manufacture procedure.

''Costs and handling still to resolve:'' Grenade quantity, carriage, resupply, action economy, target/range, duration, damage, magic-corrosion tests, and whether weapon imbuement uses a Power, installed mod, or other paid ability await collision with the SDM Quickstart and Our Golden Age. Do not silently grant unbounded extra attacks, free castings, or bypasses of Ichi's Burn and symbiosis constraints.

